1
00:03:49,376 --> 00:03:50,400
Tip # 3

2
00:03:50,656 --> 00:03:53,472
That you can sell half of your investment-

3
00:03:53,984 --> 00:03:58,151
-If you've gone with SEK 10,000, yes, sell half.

4
00:03:58,592 --> 00:04:01,408
Then you don't sell everything, so if it continues up-

5
00:04:01,664 --> 00:04:06,107
-So you are still on the train, but you reduce your possible profit.

6
00:04:06,528 --> 00:04:08,668
Then you have secured some money.

7
00:04:08,832 --> 00:04:12,416
Tip number 4, it's not to sell everything at once.

8
00:04:12,928 --> 00:04:20,493
If you have a share that has gone pretty well, as in my case where Sinch is worth SEK 200,000.

9
00:04:20,863 --> 00:04:26,309
It's not that smart if I sell everything at once, but I can go out with a little at a time.

10
00:04:42,879 --> 00:04:45,909
Tip number 5, do not sell the shares.

11
00:04:46,463 --> 00:04:51,327
You may be convinced that the company will go well or you may be wrong.

12
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:53,119
Why should you sell?

13
00:04:53,631 --> 00:04:59,415
Really wondering if it's right to sell, because in most cases-

14
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:05,764
-So it is just short -term noise, that something is happening like viruses in society or whatever.

15
00:05:05,919 --> 00:05:08,479
Which makes you doubt on your investment.

16
00:05:08,991 --> 00:05:14,825
But it is true that quite often you are actually wrong and maybe should remain.

17
00:05:18,975 --> 00:05:23,501
Alright, I'll tell you why I'm not going to sell my shares in Sinch.

18
00:05:23,583 --> 00:05:31,004
From the beginning, it was so that I heard about the company Sinch first in the pod Market Makers.
